## Authentication
Cookie-based (dashboard_token) — Authentication method detected from captured traffic.

### Providing credentials
- Prefer passing auth as request headers or cookies at call time (do not hardcode secrets into the skill).
- If executing via an external proxy/executor, pass per-call credentials (cookies and/or headers) so they are not persisted.

## Dependencies
- Runtime capable of HTTPS requests.
- If using `scripts/api.ts`: TypeScript toolchain (or transpile to JS).

## Endpoints

### Data Read (1)
- `GET /cart/{cartId}/patc-config` — Get configuration for patching a specific shopping cart.

### Search (1)
- `HEAD /suggestions` — Check for search suggestions based on a given query.

## Quick Start

### OpenClaw (Unbrowse) workflow
- Authenticate in the browser first (no credentials are shipped with this skill).
- Capture fresh auth locally: run `unbrowse_capture` on an authenticated page for this domain.
- Execute via backend gate + client browser executor: `unbrowse_replay` with `executionMode="backend"`.

Example:
```text
unbrowse_replay { service: "amazon-co-uk", executionMode: "backend", endpoint: "GET /cart/{cartId}/patc-config" }
```

```typescript
// Retrieve patching configuration for a specific cart.
async function getPatchingConfig(cartId: string) {
  try {
    const config = await client.getCartCartIdPatcConfig({ cartId });
    console.log("Patching configuration:", config);
    return config;
  } catch (error) {
    console.error("Failed to retrieve patching configuration:", error);
    return null;
  }
}
```

```typescript
// Check for search suggestions based on a query.
async function checkForSuggestions(query: string) {
  try {
    const response = await client.headSuggestions({ query });
    if (response.status === 200) {
      console.log("Search suggestions are available.");
      return true;
    } else {
      console.log("No search suggestions found.");
      return false;
    }
  } catch (error) {
    console.error("Error checking for search suggestions:", error);
    return false;
  }
}
```

